ile. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\ndocs/proposal.md:505:    P2 -->|\"Gate 3: 50% merged with no human code edits\"| P3[\"Phase 3: Scale<br/>k8s executor<br/>second repo<br/>shared roles repo<br/>budgets and digest\"]\ninternal/github/clienttest/suite.go\ninternal/github/integration_test.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83ee5ce4-848c-4479-bbba-50c03aa439df","uuid":"8aec1908-4e22-4444-8dc4-a638ff639ec1","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:13:38.097Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/TODO.md:42:- #60 Onboard a second repository\ndocs/proposal.md:440:Scanners also take `route` (`pending`, `none` or `needs-human`). Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts, 3 review rounds and worker diff thresholds of 1,000 lines (warn) and 2,000 lines (hold). Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `:`, leading `-`, `..` or spaces; an abbreviated SHA is rejected, use all 40 characters); `ard config check` reports the file and key. A worker's `timeout` and `max_budget_usd` cover the whole job (every step), and `tests: \"\"` disables its test step. Per-role keys are `every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `timeout`, `agent`, `model`, `max_budget_usd`, `budget_usd_per_day` (that role's own daily cap in USD; unset or 0 means only the repo cap applies), `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `max_test_fixes`, `max_review_rounds`, `diff_warn_lines` and `diff_max_lines` (worker roles; positive integers, 